# Root .env - read by Docker Compose only. Copy to .env if you need to change a host port.
#
# The defaults are the conventional ones and are what a reviewer on a clean machine wants.
# Override them when something already owns 8000 or 3000 locally; the containers always listen
# on 8000 and 3000 internally, so only the host side moves.
#
# API_PORT also determines the API URL baked into the UI bundle, and WEB_HOST, which the API
# uses to build its CORS origin regex. Changing one port by hand and not the other is the
# classic way to get an opaque browser network error against a server logging clean 200s.

# API_PORT=8000
# UI_PORT=3000
